  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Kulyash believes in equality.\n\nGiven an integer NNN, output a binary string of length NNN such that:\n\n\nThe count of 010101 subsequences in the string is **equal** to the count of 101010 subsequences;\nThe string has **at least** one occurrence of 000 as well as 111.\nIf multiple such strings exist, print any. Also, it is guaranteed that corresponding to the given input, an answer always exists.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line will contain TTT, number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nEach test case contains of a single line of input, an integer NNN - the length of the binary string.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output any binary string of length NNN satisfying the given conditions.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "3≤N≤10003 \\leq N \\leq 10003≤N≤1000",
      "Subtasks"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n4\n3",
        "output": "1001\n010",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: A binary string satisfying both the conditions is 100110011001. The count of 010101 as well as 101010 subsequences in the string is 222.\nTest case 222: A binary string satisfying both the conditions is 010010010. The count of 010101 as well as 101010 subsequences in the string is 111."
      }
    ]
  },
